---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const darkCode='<div style="max-width:720px"><iframe src="https://peakcountryhail.com/embed/hail-status/?theme=dark&source=embedded-widget" title="Northern Colorado Hail Status" width="100%" height="340" style="border:0" loading="lazy"></iframe></div>';
const lightCode=darkCode.replace('theme=dark','theme=light');
---
<Layout title="Northern Colorado Hail Status Widget" description="Add a lightweight Northern Colorado hail-status resource to your website with a free Peak Country iframe widget using NWS and SPC public data.">
  <header class="page-head widget-doc-head"><div class="eyebrow">A useful local weather resource</div><h1>Embed Northern Colorado hail status on your website.</h1><p>Give visitors concise current hail context without adding a radar map, account, cookie, or complicated integration.</p></header>
  <section class="section widget-doc-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">Built for local organizations</div><h2>Fast, restrained, and connected to the full tracker.</h2><p>The widget summarizes the same supported storm states used by Peak Country’s <a href="/hail-tracker/">Northern Colorado Hail Tracker</a>. It fits dealership, repair, insurance, community, club, and publication websites without presenting itself as an advertisement.</p></div><aside><strong>Important context</strong><p>The display is automated and informational. It is not an official warning service, cannot guarantee weather accuracy, and should never replace National Weather Service alerts or local emergency guidance.</p></aside></section>
  <section class="section widget-doc-preview" aria-labelledby="dark-preview"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Live preview</div><h2 id="dark-preview">Dark theme</h2></div><a href="/data-sources/">Read the data methodology →</a></div><iframe src="/embed/hail-status/?theme=dark&source=widget-documentation" title="Northern Colorado Hail Status dark theme preview" width="100%" height="340" loading="lazy"></iframe><h3>Copy and paste</h3><pre><code>{darkCode}</code></pre></section>
  <section class="section widget-doc-preview widget-doc-preview--light" aria-labelledby="light-preview"><div class="eyebrow">Alternative presentation</div><h2 id="light-preview">Light theme</h2><iframe src="/embed/hail-status/?theme=light&source=widget-documentation" title="Northern Colorado Hail Status light theme preview" width="100%" height="340" loading="lazy"></iframe><h3>Copy and paste</h3><pre><code>{lightCode}</code></pre></section>
  <section class="section widget-doc-details"><div><div class="eyebrow">Privacy by design</div><h2>No visitor profile required.</h2><p>The widget does not request personal information, set cookies, use local storage, or fingerprint visitors. Its optional <code>source</code> parameter adds ordinary campaign attribution only to the outbound Hail Tracker link.</p></div><div><div class="eyebrow">Partner-ready URL</div><h2>Use one safe source slug.</h2><p>Replace <code>embedded-widget</code> with a short identifier containing only lowercase letters, numbers, hyphens, or underscores—for example, <code>source=acme-auto</code>. Invalid values fall back safely to <code>embedded-widget</code>.</p><p><a class="button" href="/hail-tracker/">View Full Hail Tracker →</a></p></div></section>
  <div class="widget-doc-mountains" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <style>
    .widget-doc-head{background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgb(4 18 31/.94),rgb(6 29 48/.76)),url('/brand/hero-storm-background-1942.webp') center/cover}.widget-doc-intro,.widget-doc-details{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:clamp(2rem,6vw,6rem)}.widget-doc-intro aside{padding-left:2rem;border-left:2px solid var(--cyan)}.widget-doc-preview{background:#eef4f6}.widget-doc-preview--light{background-image:url('/images/longs-peak-topographic-background-light.svg');background-size:1100px}.widget-doc-preview iframe{display:block;max-width:720px;margin:2rem auto;border:0}.widget-doc-preview pre{overflow:auto;max-width:900px;padding:1.25rem;color:#dceaf1;background:#071b2b;border-left:3px solid var(--cyan);white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word}.widget-doc-preview code{font-size:.78rem}.widget-doc-details code{padding:.1em .35em;background:#e8eff2}.widget-doc-mountains{height:clamp(90px,14vw,190px);background:#071522 url('/brand/peak-country-approved-mountain-ridge.png') bottom center/auto 100% no-repeat}@media(max-width:700px){.widget-doc-intro,.widget-doc-details{grid-template-columns:1fr}.widget-doc-intro aside{padding:1.25rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--cyan);border-left:0}.widget-doc-preview{padding-inline:1rem}.widget-doc-preview iframe{height:340px}}
  </style>
</Layout>
